invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_hw.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_hw.c's use_vaes answers 1 before ch_cfg.cpu exists to carry
  the caller's CH_CPU_VAES bit, so every x86-64 AES=hw and AES=runtime
  object hands its blocks to the VAES kernels and dies of SIGILL on a CPU
  with AES-NI and PCLMULQDQ and without VAES, which the AES=runtime answer
  admits. Every vector and equivalence case passes on a CPU with the
  instructions.
  The script compiles gcm_hw.c for x86-64 and requires its object to call
  no kernel.

--- old
static int use_vaes(void) {
    return 0;
}
--- new
static int use_vaes(void) {
    return 1;
}
